{"id": "P08338", "name": "Stephen Saad", "name_chinese": "Stephen Saad", "country": "South Africa", "net_worth_usd_m": "962.7", "net_worth_source": "Forbes real-time (former)", "source_of_wealth": "pharmaceuticals", "industry": "healthcare", "sec_insider_companies": "", "shared_with": "", "appears_on": "Forbes real-time (former) (2021); Forbes annual (2013-2018); Hurun Global (2015-2018)", "focus": [], "forbes_profile_url": "https://www.forbes.com/profile/stephen-saad/", "wikidata_url": "", "forbes_bio": ["Stephen Saad founded South Africa's largest pharmaceuticals maker, Aspen Pharmacare, in 1997.", "Traded on the Johannesburg Stock Exchange, Aspen Pharmacare markets generic medicines in 150 countries.", "Saad is the chief executive and head of Aspen's board.", "He became a millionaire at age 29 when he sold his share in the drug business Covan Zurich for $3 million.", "In October 2016, Saad won the Entrepreneur of the Year award at the All Africa Business Leaders Awards gala."], "forbes_facts": ["In 2012, Saad became chairman of The Sharks, a Durban rugby team.", "He spends his free time at Exeter, his private game reserve at Sabi Sands, which is adjacent to Kruger National Park, the largest national park in South Africa."]}
